more("para1", [["Parasitic zoonoses in India: why they matter", "Hydatidosis, cysticercosis, toxoplasmosis, toxocariosis, giardiosis, cryptosporidiosis, leishmaniosis, scabies and zoonotic fascioliosis are among the parasitic zoonoses that veterinarians help to control. The links are dogs and stray animals, undercooked meat, contaminated water and vegetables, and vectors. This is why the chapter on public health in your syllabus keeps returning to parasites."]]);
more("para5", [["Calendar thinking for control", "Parasites follow the seasons. Flukes and paramphistomes rise after the monsoon because snails multiply. Haemonchus peaks in warm, humid weather. Ticks surge in the rains. Coccidiosis hits when litter is wet. A control plan written on a calendar, with the weakest point of each cycle marked, is more useful than a list of drugs."]]);

